# Go build output
/dossierx
/dossierx.exe
*.exe
/dist/

# Test/coverage output
*.out
coverage.html

# Engine artifacts left behind by running the CLI against a fixture.
# "dossierx check" writes .dossierx-comment-digest.json next to a project's
# config, so every fixture render and every sample-viewer regeneration drops
# one. In THIS repo they are always regenerable droppings — nothing here is a
# dossierx project whose review history we keep (no .dossierx-* store is
# tracked). A real consuming project still commits its own digest; its .gitignore
# is its own. Unanchored so it catches the repo root, testdata fixtures, and any
# project checked out inside this tree.
.dossierx-comment-digest.json

# ...with one exception. testdata/fixture-graph-demo is the first fixture in this
# repo that IS a ledger-covered dossierx project: it carries 25 locked claims, so
# its lock store is ledger-covered, and a ledger-covered project without a
# committed digest store makes "dossierx check" emit comment-digest-absent and
# exit 1. A fresh clone or CI checkout would fail on it. The digest is therefore
# a tracked input of that fixture, exactly as a real consuming project commits
# its own.
!testdata/fixture-graph-demo/.dossierx-comment-digest.json

